# `git archive` (and so a GitHub "Download ZIP" or release tarball) fills in the
# describe placeholder in pyproject.toml's [tool.versioningit.vcs] table with the
# output of `git describe --tags` for the archived commit. That is how a build from
# an archive, which has no .git directory, still reports the real version instead
# of "0+unknown". See the comment above that table.
pyproject.toml export-subst
